; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Eight-Point Star Tiles
; CATEGORY: Patterns & Mandalas
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     tessellation, star, geometric art, grid, filled
; SUMMARY:  Tiles the screen with eight-pointed stars whose tips touch, leaving cross shapes between them, in the style of Islamic geometric art.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   An eight-pointed star is two squares, one turned 45 degrees.
;   Placed on a grid so that the tips of neighbors just touch, the
;   stars leave cross-shaped spaces between them. Each star gets an
;   octagon in its heart and each cross a small diamond, the way
;   tiles are often set in old mosques and palaces.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Change CELL for bigger or smaller tiles, or change the
;   four colors at the top.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * a star outline as 16 points, taking turns between two radii
;   * working out the inner radius so the star's edges are straight
;   * a square grid where shapes touch exactly
;   * points on a circle with SIN and COS
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Shrink the stars a little (RADIUS less than half of CELL). What
;     shape do the spaces between them become?
;   * Try a six-pointed star (12 points) on the same grid.
;   * Swap the star and background colors.
; ============================================================

make "cell 100
make "radius :cell / 2              ; tips of neighbors just touch
make "stargold [230 180 60]
make "ground [25 50 100]
make "heart [40 150 150]
make "jewel [200 60 70]

; Inner corners of an 8-point star made of two squares sit at
; R x cos 45 / cos 22.5 from the center, which keeps every edge straight.
make "inner :radius * (cos 45) / (cos 22.5)

; A filled polygon through points on circles round (x, y).
; :radii takes turns, so [R r] gives a star and [R] a regular polygon.
to roundshape :x :y :points :radii :turn :color
  localmake "pts map [cornerpoint :x :y 360 * ? / :points + :turn ~
                      item 1 + remainder ? count :radii :radii] iseq 0 :points - 1
  penup setpos first :pts pendown
  filled :color [foreach butfirst :pts [setpos ?] setpos first :pts]
end

to cornerpoint :x :y :angle :r
  output list :x + :r * sin :angle :y + :r * cos :angle
end

; Later drawing covers earlier drawing, so each star goes down first
; and the small shapes that sit on top (octagon, diamond) come after.
to tiling
  for [row -3 3] [
    for [col -4 4] [
      localmake "x :col * :cell
      localmake "y :row * :cell
      roundshape :x :y 16 (list :radius :inner) 0 :stargold
      roundshape :x :y 8 (list :radius * 0.42) 22.5 :heart
      roundshape :x + :cell / 2 :y + :cell / 2 4 (list :cell * 0.14) 0 :jewel
    ]
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground :ground
setpencolor [250 240 220]
setpensize 2
tiling
